[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3251406358","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110242#issuecomment-3251406358","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110242","id":3251406358,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BzIYW","user":{"login":"ktxyz","id":67782157,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NzgyMTU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67782157?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz","html_url":"https://github.com/ktxyz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-04T01:49:48Z","updated_at":"2025-09-04T01:53:07Z","body":"Other simple solutions would be adding some additional `uid_scan` flag or checking `EditorFileSystem::get_singleton() != nullptr` but I'm not a fan since they would increase mantainance cost of a silence for a single warning per runtime.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3251406358/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3253428270","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110242#issuecomment-3253428270","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110242","id":3253428270,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7B62Au","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-04T12:19:07Z","updated_at":"2025-09-04T12:19:07Z","body":"> checking EditorFileSystem::get_singleton() != nullptr\r\n\r\nThat would be the simplest solution here. A side-effect is that it makes the warning not print in the situation when the crash would occur, but it's super edge case anyway. The warning shows correctly once the filesystem cache exists.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3253428270/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3253534382","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110242#issuecomment-3253534382","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110242","id":3253534382,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7B7P6u","user":{"login":"ktxyz","id":67782157,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NzgyMTU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67782157?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz","html_url":"https://github.com/ktxyz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-04T12:46:03Z","updated_at":"2025-09-04T12:52:49Z","body":"> > checking EditorFileSystem::get_singleton() != nullptr\r\n> \r\n> That would be the simplest solution here. A side-effect is that it makes the warning not print in the situation when the crash would occur, but it's super edge case anyway. The warning shows correctly once the filesystem cache exists.\r\n\r\nYeah to keep warning guard that would be the simplest solution and I agree the crash overall is a rare corner edge. But to me it seems that this guard breaks the initialization a bit - at least design wise. I might be wrong as I'm just getting familiar with overall code base but from the code flow I assume `EditorFileSystem` static functions in that code path were designed not to rely on `EditorFileSystem` instance so they could be used during setup phase.\r\n\r\nThat guard kinda breaks this idea and introduces dependency on `EditorFileSystem` instancing during `Main::setup2` where we know for 100% it's not going to be valid.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3253534382/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3253574377","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110242#issuecomment-3253574377","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110242","id":3253574377,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7B7Zrp","user":{"login":"ktxyz","id":67782157,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NzgyMTU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67782157?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz","html_url":"https://github.com/ktxyz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-04T12:55:55Z","updated_at":"2025-09-04T12:57:59Z","body":"So as I see in the long run this is a choice between:\r\n\r\n1. Revert guard and handle the warning differently later on\r\n2. Add null check and later on move `EditorFileSystem` initialization to `Main::setup2`\r\n   * I mean it could just be left out but why keep workarounds for crashes instead of fixing the root issues\r\n\r\nThe second approach is probably a larger effort but I also don't see why `EditorFileSystem` needs to be a Node instead of core/semi-core singleton if it handles `Main::setup2` initialization as well.\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3253574377/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3254468749","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110242#issuecomment-3254468749","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110242","id":3254468749,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7B-0CN","user":{"login":"ktxyz","id":67782157,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NzgyMTU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67782157?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz","html_url":"https://github.com/ktxyz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ktxyz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-04T16:15:22Z","updated_at":"2025-09-04T16:15:22Z","body":"Anyway, if null check is prefered from removing the guard\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nif (EditorFileSystem::get_singleton() == nullptr || EditorFileSystem::get_singleton()->first_scan)\r\n```\r\n\r\nmakes the warning print in the situation when the crash would occur.\r\n ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3254468749/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":